  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS - Mali (01-Oct-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mali, HIV, Plan International, Inc. (Plan Mali)This program has the following goals: Protect the rights of PLHIV and specific groups.  Reduce new HIV infections by 50 percent.  Reduce PLHIV mortality by 50 percent within the framework of universal access to treatment, care and support. The objectives of this program are: 70 percent of monitored PLHIV are integrated into the health/dignity prevention program to reduce the spread of HIV by 2017..  At least 60 percent of bridge populations linked to key populations are adopting safer behavior by 2017 (miners, prisoners, etc.). NSF 2013-2017, page 68, indicator 1.2.  At least 75 percent of key populations are adopting safer behavior by 2017 (SWs, MSM, people who inject drugs)..  New cases of STIs are reduced by 50 percent by 2017.</narrative>
  </description>
